				24,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(build): Restructure build flags and add compile environment support\n\n- Introduced `CompileEnv` constant and corresponding `Compile` CLI argument to handle compilation-specific configurations in Mountain's build system\n- Reordered flag processing sequence (Bundle before Clean) to align with standard build pipeline flow\n- Added explicit compile flag handling that appends \"Compile\" to product name and bundle ID when enabled\n- Maintains debug logging consistency while improving build script maintainability\n\nThis restructuring supports upcoming build optimization requirements for Land's MVP Path A deliverables, particularly:\n1. Preparing for incremental compilation strategies in Tauri-based builds\n2. Enabling clearer separation between bundling/compilation/clean phases\n3. Enhancing cross-platform build configuration capabilities through environment variables\n\nPart of ongoing Maintain element improvements following commit 9e19fb4 (build ignore patterns) and 3d73508 (build system refactor)",
